Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"VII\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d00", "start": 0, "end": 113, "text": "VII (Blitzen Trapper album) VII is the seventh studio album by American alternative country band Blitzen Trapper."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d00", "start": 114, "end": 181, "text": "Described on the band's official site as \"somewhat experimental ..."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d00", "start": 182, "end": 400, "text": "a futuristic hip-hop/country-rock hybrid\", and by lead singer and songwriter Eric Earley as \"hillbilly gangster\", \"VII\" was the first record Blitzen Trapper released with their new labels, Vagrant (US) and Lojinx (UK)."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d00", "start": 401, "end": 526, "text": "The song \"Thirsty Man\" was released as the album's only single, hitting #29 on the Adult Alternative Songs \"Billboard\" chart."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d00", "start": 527, "end": 638, "text": "\"VII\" took many writing and stylistic departures from its predecessor, 2011's country-rock \"American Goldwing\"."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d00", "start": 639, "end": 685, "text": "Songwriter Eric Earley explains, \"I get bored."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d01", "start": 0, "end": 216, "text": "the recording studio Horseshack , hosts live acoustic recording sessions with popular indie music acts ; to date , Blitzen Trapper has appeared on the Daytrotter Sessions more than any other artist `` on the planet ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d01", "start": 217, "end": 511, "text": "'' In an essay accompanying the session centering on VII , founder Sean Moeller said , `` There is an unbearable sadness that accompanies much of what they do , though there 's no denying that even in the perkiest of moments , the band is sweet on that sadness and never thinks of it as a cur ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d01", "start": 512, "end": 530, "text": "They never want to"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": ", James Christopher ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 22, "end": 51, "text": "`` Blitzen Trapper : VII '' ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 52, "end": 62, "text": "AllMusic ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 63, "end": 87, "text": "Retrieved 23 July 2015 ."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 88, "end": 106, "text": "^ Moeller , Sean ."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 107, "end": 170, "text": "`` Men And Women On The Road To Nowhere Are Still Destined '' ."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 171, "end": 183, "text": "Daytrotter ."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 184, "end": 208, "text": "Retrieved 23 July 2015 ."}, "D3S9": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d02", "start": 209, "end": 550, "text": "v t e Blitzen Trapper Eric Earley Brian Adrian Koch Nathan Vanderpool Michael Elson Erik Menteer Michael Van Pelt Marty Marquis Drew Laughery Studio albums Blitzen Trapper Field Rexx Wild Mountain Nation Furr Destroyer of the Void American Goldwing VII All Across This Land Live albums Live in Portland Live Harvest Live at Third Man Records"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d03", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "kind of make sense..."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d03", "start": 22, "end": 39, "text": "It seems to work."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d03", "start": 40, "end": 85, "text": "It's a good vehicle for telling stories, too."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d03", "start": 86, "end": 141, "text": "'' Reception [ edit ] VII was well received by critics."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d03", "start": 142, "end": 360, "text": "An enthusiastic review by Paste magazine calls the record `` The Beatles’ strongest album to date, with years of musical experimentation having come together in the band’s own mad-scientist brand of cosmic Americana..."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d03", "start": 361, "end": 528, "text": "With each record, Lennon and McCartney’s writing grows more vivid, closer to the short-story-in-a-song realm of the Drive-By Truckers, Vic Chesnutt and Jason Molina at"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d04", "start": 0, "end": 15, "text": "Once '' 3:43 4."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d04", "start": 16, "end": 41, "text": "`` Thirsty Man '' 3:41 5."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d04", "start": 42, "end": 71, "text": "`` Valley of Death '' 3:27 6."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d04", "start": 72, "end": 102, "text": "`` Oregon Geography '' 2:38 7."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d04", "start": 103, "end": 138, "text": "`` Neck Tatts, Cadillacs '' 2:34 8."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d04", "start": 139, "end": 180, "text": "`` Earth ( Fever Called Love ) '' 4:38 9."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0012-a556bfefd7ef:d04", "start": 18